WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.293
Step 3 collects OCI from the
day-one fixtures: four notices,

2
00:00:04.293 --> 00:00:08.625
three open, one needing action,
all valid against the schema.

3
00:00:08.625 --> 00:00:10.625
Step 4 reads the records.

4
00:00:10.625 --> 00:00:14.675
Look at the resources column: that's why
the kit makes a get per announcement.

5
00:00:14.675 --> 00:00:19.775
The maintenance names a database system,
with its window starting November 22.

6
00:00:19.775 --> 00:00:25.003
The change names a load balancer, and
it's action required by December 15,

7
00:00:25.003 --> 00:00:27.750
by Oracle's own type, not by any kit rule.

8
00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:31.415
The advisory is open, and the
incident is already closed,

9
00:00:31.415 --> 00:00:33.725
because Oracle marked it inactive.

10
00:00:33.725 --> 00:00:36.405
Because both name the agency's resources,

11
00:00:36.405 --> 00:00:40.250
Chapter 6 can route each one to
the owners of those systems.
